<blockquote>
<p>Subjects consuming SCP-1622 in this fashion demonstrate no unusual behaviors aside from a marked dislike of other cheeses. This is believed to be due to the superior flavor of SCP-1622, and is not considered anomalous.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds crazy anomalous to me. I would be very surprised if blue whale milk produces particularly tasty cheese, and in any event, a lot of a cheese's quality comes from its creation and treatment. It would be quite possible to ruin even a superb cheese with poor preparation. Moreover, there's no linear scale of cheeses. I like certain cheeses for munching, but they'd be terrible in, say, pizza. So I don't know why the article is treating the cheese's flavor like it's nonanomalous, when it's just as obviously anomalous as the slapping. Plus, I don't buy the ability to calculate the cost of preparing and presenting to the cent.</p>
<p>I get the idea (haughty cheese), but the presentation is too careless for me to upvote.</p>

